## Locale and Invoice Reminder Timing

Cron-sent emails use each recipient's configured locale. Check custom templates in the languages your clients use.

In invoice settings, **Send Payment Reminders At** accepts `HH:MM` in the configured timezone. Before-due and after-due reminders are sent on the first cron run at or after that time. Leave the field empty to send on the first cron run after midnight. Keep cron running regularly; reminder day intervals still determine which invoices are eligible.

## Storage Location

Templates exist in two places:

1. **Module source** — `modules/{Module}/templates/email/`
2. **Database** — `email_template` table (copied there when module is installed)

Edit installed templates in the admin panel. To restore defaults from the module files, see [Reset Built-in Templates](#reset-built-in-templates).

## Limitations

- Variables only appear in the **Variables** tab after an email has been sent at least once
- Email client HTML support varies — test with popular clients
- Inline CSS works more reliably than `<style>` blocks

## Example Module

See the [core email templates](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/tree/main/src/modules/Email/templates/email) for more template examples.
